output/

**.bak
*.local.*
!**/README.md
.kitchen/

*.nupkg
*.suo
*.user
*.coverage
.vs
.psproj
.sln
markdownissues.txt
node_modules
package-lock.json

# Real tenant data must never be staged. docs/examples/ is allowlisted: add an explicit
# negation below for each example that is genuinely meant to be tracked.
docs/examples/*
!docs/examples/example-structure.json
!docs/examples/README.md

# Internal planning and design material: session plans, design specs and audit reports. These are
# working notes, not documentation -- some record what was verified against a live tenant, and all
# of them describe the module as it was mid-development rather than as it ships. They were left out
# of this repository when it was seeded and stay on the maintainer's disk, ignored. The reasoning
# they carry is not lost: where a house rule exists because something failed, the explanation lives
# in docs/development/rationale.md. Add an explicit negation below for a file genuinely meant to be
# tracked.
docs/superpowers/

# Export-OERInventory run bundles, wherever they land in a clone.
# The folder is named oer-inventory-<tenant>-<stamp> (Export-OERInventory.ps1:194).
oer-inventory-*/
inventory.json

# docs/live-verification/ is where live tenant console output gets pasted in on purpose, and no
# rule above has ever reached it. Redaction happens on the way INTO a checklist (see
# docs/live-verification/README.md, gated by tests/QA/dochygiene.tests.ps1); these two rules cover
# the raw material that redaction is done FROM, so an unredacted transcript cannot be staged by a
# stray `git add docs/`.
docs/live-verification/raw/
docs/live-verification/*.log

# Claude Code's per-clone session state -- machine-local session ids and absolute temp paths, of no
# value to anyone else and stale the moment it is shared.
.claude/

# Neither block untracks anything: .gitignore never does. The checklists under
# docs/live-verification/ stay tracked deliberately -- they are the verification record, and only
# the raw material beside them is ignored.
